gner_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"6832dc02fdd35b8a53037791063a30e0bae7a668e7cce113f4ebd382913cbe00","event_uuid":"ee59cedb-1231-4f6b-8c2b-2fdda94391af","position":{"commit_sha":"0ed0b3f9d7dc84a68aaea367d50aa11fce7b9a3c","position":"1787311710564398001-ee59cedb-1231-4f6b-8c2b-2fdda94391af"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"e9b85475e48e41df98731175943d1706ca60c29e55843007cb9ef9bba4e1cd6c","event_uuid":"78271d7a-9fed-4b7c-aa83-a214e9d9df00","position":{"commit_sha":"0ed0b3f9d7dc84a68aaea367d50aa11fce7b9a3c","position":"1787311712572310001-78271d7a-9fed-4b7c-aa83-a214e9d9df00"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-238_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"eff19c3d-071a-47b5-bae6-8b48a3343a8c","comments":[],"created_at":1787311480099046001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"3ef93cc3-766d-4411-8171-da0633af3ecd","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"0e1d-c698-c38d-4c3e"},{"link_uuid":"7bf7e4e2-9699-43f9-b2f2-073adf4589aa","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"8359-9a62-055f-4811"}],"description":"## The defect\n\n`tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_programmatic_e2e_heldout.py::test_check_access_returns_a_typed_six_step_result`\nfails intermittently with `assert 'FAIL' == 'PASS'` — the bridge access-check oracle reports a\nstep as FAIL in a full-suite run, and passes when its tier is run alone.\n\n**Observed twice, by two independent sessions, on different days and different suite sizes:**\n\n* Session log `skeletal-soaplike-caracal` (`8359-9a62-055f-4811`): *\"Local full suite (bare\n  pytest, matching CI): 13683 passed, 1 failed — test_check_access_returns_a_typed_six_step_result\n  in tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_programmatic_e2e_heldout.py (Jira bridge…)\"*\n* During bug `0e1d-c698-c38d-4c3e`: `pytest tests/unit tests/interfaces tests/integration -q` gave\n  **14156 passed, 55 skipped, 1 xfailed, 1 failed**, that same test, same `'FAIL' == 'PASS'`\n  assertion. Re-running `pytest tests/interfaces -q` alone: **1958 passed, 0 failed**, that test\n  included.\n\nPasses in isolation, fails in the larger run — the signature of cross-tier pollution (shared\nstate, env, or ordering) rather than a defect in the assertion itself. The test shells out toward\na Jira instance, so an environment/credential dependency that some other tier mutates is a\nleading candidate, but that is a **hypothesis, not a finding** — nobody has root-caused it.\n\n## Why this is a bug and not a retry\n\n`AGENTS.md`: *\"A flaky test is a BUG to root-cause, never a retry.\"* A test that fails\nintermittently in the full suite is exactly the oracle CI depends on. Until it is diagnosed, every\nfuture agent that hits it must decide whether it is real, and the honest answer today is \"nobody\nknows\" — which is what makes it expensive.\n\nIt has been observed twice and recorded **only in session logs**, which are not work items and do\nnot surface in `ready` / `next-batch`. That is why it keeps being re-discovered instead of fixed.\n\n## Why it was not fixed in scope\n\nFound while proving bug `0e1d-c698-c38d-4c3e` (live-DC pass-health fail-open). It is unrelated:\nthe test imports nothing from `tests/_child_diag.py` or `tests/external/live_jira_dc/`, and it also\npredates that change (`skeletal-soaplike-caracal` observed it earlier). It is also outside that\nticket's file lane.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The failure is reproduced DETERMINISTICALLY — the specific ordering, tier combination, or\n      shared state that triggers it is identified, and it can be made to fail on demand.\n- [ ] The root cause is a named changeable artifact, not \"flakiness\" or \"an environment issue\".\n- [ ] A RED test or a seeded reproduction proves the mechanism before the fix.\n- [ ] The fix addresses the CLASS (the shared state / ordering dependency), not just this one\n      test — if another test shares the seam, it is swept.\n- [ ] The full suite passes repeatedly (not once) after the fix.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","8359-9a62-055f-4811"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"ee59cedb-1231-4f6b-8c2b-2fdda94391af","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"2c4b-3cd9-8bb0-4493","ticket_type":"bug","title":"test_check_access_...six_step_result is flaky in full-suite runs","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["82396d7c-c452-4c23-be76-bafa011c7e90","3ef93cc3-766d-4411-8171-da0633af3ecd","7bf7e4e2-9699-43f9-b2f2-073adf4589aa","ee59cedb-1231-4f6b-8c2b-2fdda94391af","78271d7a-9fed-4b7c-aa83-a214e9d9df00"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787313691891642001,"uuid":"17931016-9915-4c99-973e-891ce110cec2"}